WEBVTT

00:00:00.029 --> 00:00:01.542
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:01.548 --> 00:00:03.123
Let's say good night to your brother.

00:00:03.327 --> 00:00:04.391
Night, Sam.

00:00:04.516 --> 00:00:05.901
Hey, Dean.

00:00:05.926 --> 00:00:07.462
Daddy! Hey, buddy.

00:00:08.386 --> 00:00:10.000
Sweet dreams, Sam.

00:00:14.174 --> 00:00:16.662
Dad's missing. I need
you to help me find him.

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:18.617
The trail for dad, it's getting colder.

00:00:18.742 --> 00:00:21.342
Every day. You don't think I want
to find dad as much as you do?

00:00:21.366 --> 00:00:22.750
I know you do. Find dad.

00:00:22.774 --> 00:00:25.076
Mom's gone. She isn't coming back.

00:00:27.576 --> 00:00:29.495
Don't talk about her like that.

00:00:52.781 --> 00:00:54.041
Mommy?

00:00:55.707 --> 00:00:57.644
Hey, sweetie.

00:00:57.921 --> 00:01:01.886
Why aren't you in bed?
There's something in my closet.

00:01:17.768 --> 00:01:18.611
See?

00:01:18.646 --> 00:01:19.930
There's nothing there.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:24.264
You're sure? I'm sure.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:32.586
Now, come on.

00:01:32.696 --> 00:01:33.701
Into bed.

00:01:41.174 --> 00:01:42.804
I don't like this house.

00:01:43.421 --> 00:01:45.026
You're just not used to it yet.

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:51.717
But you and your brother and me,
we are going to be very happy here.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.282
I promise.

00:01:55.898 --> 00:01:57.560
I love you.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.147
The chair.

00:02:07.032 --> 00:02:08.451
Okay.

00:02:09.093 --> 00:02:10.075
Right.

00:02:13.965 --> 00:02:15.023
The chair.

00:02:17.655 --> 00:02:19.355
Just to be safe.

00:02:51.724 --> 00:02:55.274
Please, god, don't let it be rats.

00:03:15.062 --> 00:03:16.304
Terrific.

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:15.063
All right.

00:05:15.088 --> 00:05:16.892
I've been cruising some websites.

00:05:16.997 --> 00:05:19.401
Think I found a few
candidates for our next gig.

00:05:20.713 --> 00:05:23.481
A fishing trawler found
off the coast of Cali.

00:05:23.579 --> 00:05:25.011
Its crew vanished.

00:05:25.242 --> 00:05:28.739
And we got some cattle
mutilations in west Texas.

00:05:29.223 --> 00:05:29.843
Hey!

00:05:31.682 --> 00:05:33.752
Am I boring you with
this hunting-Evil stuff?

00:05:34.295 --> 00:05:36.385
No, I'm listening. Keep going.

00:05:38.398 --> 00:05:41.185
And here a Sacramento man
shot himself in the head...

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:42.869
Three times.

00:05:45.317 --> 00:05:47.368
Any of these things
blowing up your skirt, pal?

00:05:51.413 --> 00:05:53.455
Wait, I've seen this. Seen what?

00:06:00.344 --> 00:06:01.461
What are you doing?

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:11.583
Dean, I know where we have to go next.

00:06:11.801 --> 00:06:12.297
Where?

00:06:12.929 --> 00:06:13.871
Back home.

00:06:14.688 --> 00:06:15.716
Back to Kansas.

00:06:17.116 --> 00:06:18.998
Okay, random. Where'd that come from?

00:06:19.884 --> 00:06:20.900
All right, um...

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.278
This photo was taken in
front of our old house, right?

00:06:23.364 --> 00:06:24.584
The house where mom died?

00:06:26.034 --> 00:06:26.693
Yeah.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:29.945
It didn't burn down right? I mean not
completely, they rebuilt it, right?

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:32.384
I guess so, yeah. What the
hell are you talking about?

00:06:32.415 --> 00:06:34.634
Okay, look, this is gonna sound crazy,

00:06:34.664 --> 00:06:36.755
But the people who
live in our old house,

00:06:38.028 --> 00:06:39.674
I think they might be in danger.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:42.400
Why would you think that? Uh...

00:06:42.458 --> 00:06:44.488
Just, um... look, just...

00:06:44.502 --> 00:06:45.878
You got to trust me on this, okay?

00:06:47.521 --> 00:06:49.599
Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa. Trust you? Yeah.

00:06:50.119 --> 00:06:52.030
You got to give me a
little bit more than that.

00:06:52.076 --> 00:06:53.815
I can't really explain, it is all.

00:06:54.021 --> 00:06:56.555
Well, tough. I'm not going
anywhere until you do.

00:07:01.236 --> 00:07:02.939
I have these nightmares.

00:07:03.241 --> 00:07:04.651
I've noticed.

00:07:06.319 --> 00:07:09.456
And sometimes they come true.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:13.532
Come again?

00:07:14.399 --> 00:07:15.080
Look, Dean...

00:07:16.278 --> 00:07:17.748
I dreamt about Jessica's death

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:20.470
For days before it happened.

00:07:23.079 --> 00:07:25.834
Sane people have weird dreams, man.
I'm sure it's just a coincidence.

00:07:26.386 --> 00:07:29.532
No, I dreamt about the blood dripping,
her on the ceiling, the fire, everything,

00:07:29.544 --> 00:07:31.419
And I didn't do anything
'cause I didn't believe it.

00:07:31.477 --> 00:07:33.103
Now I'm dreaming about that tree,

00:07:33.273 --> 00:07:36.135
About our house, and some woman
inside screaming for help. I mean,

00:07:36.325 --> 00:07:38.775
That's where it all started, man.
This has to mean something, right?

00:07:41.059 --> 00:07:41.896
I don't know.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.109
What do you mean you
don't know, Dean? This...

00:07:45.228 --> 00:07:46.924
This woman might be in danger.

00:07:46.983 --> 00:07:51.139
This might be the thing that killed mom and
Jessica. All right, just slow down,would you?

00:07:55.191 --> 00:07:57.805
I mean, first you're telling
me that you've got this Shining

00:07:59.019 --> 00:08:00.903
and then you tell me that
I've got to go back home,

00:08:02.151 --> 00:08:03.078
Especially when...

00:08:05.069 --> 00:08:06.178
When what?

00:08:07.601 --> 00:08:09.897
When I swore to myself that
I would never go back there.

00:08:21.344 --> 00:08:23.299
Dean, we have to check this out.

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:25.855
Just to make sure.

00:08:33.213 --> 00:08:34.308
I know we do.

00:08:52.821 --> 00:08:54.427
You gonna be all right, man?

00:08:56.336 --> 00:08:58.169
Let me get back to you on that.

00:09:06.274 --> 00:09:06.769
Yes?

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:08.405
Sorry to bother you, ma'am,

00:09:08.517 --> 00:09:10.919
But we're with the
federal... I'm Sam Winchester

00:09:11.154 --> 00:09:12.921
And this is my brother, Dean.

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:15.329
Um...we used to live here.

00:09:16.248 --> 00:09:18.627
You know, we were just driving by, and

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:21.071
We were wondering if we
could come see the old place.

00:09:21.132 --> 00:09:22.298
Winchester...

00:09:23.841 --> 00:09:25.302
That is so funny.

00:09:25.499 --> 00:09:28.832
You know, I, I think I found some
of your photos the other night.

00:09:28.879 --> 00:09:29.527
You did?

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:35.968
Okay. Come on in.

00:09:47.956 --> 00:09:50.030
Juice, juice, juice!

00:09:50.065 --> 00:09:51.990
Juice, juice,  juice!

00:09:52.013 --> 00:09:55.900
That's Richie. He's
kind of a juice junkie.

00:09:56.140 --> 00:09:59.119
But, hey, at least he won't get scurvy.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:01.486
Sari,

00:10:01.899 --> 00:10:04.007
This is Sam and Dean.

00:10:04.056 --> 00:10:05.998
They used to live here. Hi.

00:10:06.528 --> 00:10:07.470
Hey, Sari.

00:10:08.425 --> 00:10:09.732
So, you just moved in?

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:11.522
Uh, yeah, from Wichita.

00:10:11.625 --> 00:10:13.051
You got family here?

00:10:14.146 --> 00:10:16.124
No, I just, uh...

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:20.464
Um, needed a fresh start. That's all.

00:10:21.598 --> 00:10:23.808
So new town,

00:10:23.918 --> 00:10:25.040
New job

00:10:25.225 --> 00:10:27.065
I mean, as soon as I find one,

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:28.739
New house.

00:10:30.802 --> 00:10:32.570
So, how you liking it so far?

00:10:34.059 --> 00:10:37.556
Well, uh, all due respect
to your childhood home,

00:10:37.649 --> 00:10:41.108
I mean, I'm sure you have
lots of happy memories here,

00:10:41.567 --> 00:10:43.850
But this place has its issues.

00:10:44.126 --> 00:10:45.341
What do you mean?

00:10:46.719 --> 00:10:48.523
Well, it's just getting old

00:10:48.928 --> 00:10:51.062
Like, the wiring, you know? We've got

00:10:51.191 --> 00:10:53.307
Flickering lights almost hourly.

00:10:53.418 --> 00:10:54.669
Oh, that's too bad.

00:10:55.148 --> 00:10:56.178
What else?

00:10:56.527 --> 00:11:00.853
Um...sink's backed up.
There's rats in the basement.

00:11:02.971 --> 00:11:04.407
I'm sorry.

00:11:04.572 --> 00:11:06.688
I don't mean to complain. No.

00:11:06.762 --> 00:11:10.166
Have you seen the rats or
have you just heard scratching?

00:11:11.252 --> 00:11:14.306
Just the scratching, actually. Mom?

00:11:18.722 --> 00:11:21.740
Ask them if it was here
when they lived here.

00:11:23.139 --> 00:11:24.188
What, Sari?

00:11:24.979 --> 00:11:26.709
The thing in my closet.

00:11:26.739 --> 00:11:31.043
Oh, no, baby, there was
nothing in their closets.

00:11:31.197 --> 00:11:32.002
Right?

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:35.086
Right, no.No, of course not.

00:11:36.353 --> 00:11:38.977
She had a nightmare the other night.

00:11:39.092 --> 00:11:40.611
I wasn't dreaming.

00:11:40.796 --> 00:11:44.226
It came into my bedroom,
and it was on fire.

00:11:45.223 --> 00:11:48.170
You heard that ? A figure on fire.

00:11:48.494 --> 00:11:50.851
And that woman Jenny, that was
the woman in your dreams? Yeah.

00:11:50.924 --> 00:11:53.685
And you hear what she was talking
about ? Scratching, flickering lights ?

00:11:53.761 --> 00:11:55.994
Both signs of a malevolent
spirit. Yeah well.

00:11:56.109 --> 00:11:58.257
I'm just freaked out your
weirdo visions are coming true.

00:11:58.273 --> 00:11:59.448
Forget about that for a minute.

00:11:59.461 --> 00:12:02.325
The thing in the house, do you think it's the
thing that killed mom and Jessica? I don't know!

00:12:02.552 --> 00:12:04.595
Has it come back or has it
been there the whole time?

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:06.955
Maybe it's something else
entirely. Sam, we don't know yet.

00:12:06.964 --> 00:12:08.745
Those people are in danger, Dean.

00:12:09.163 --> 00:12:11.139
We have to get them out
of that house. And we will.

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:12.987
No, I mean now. And how
you're gonna do that ?

00:12:13.004 --> 00:12:15.642
You got a story she's gonna believe?
Then what are we supposed to do?!

00:12:16.181 --> 00:12:17.915
We just got to chill out, that's all.

00:12:18.774 --> 00:12:21.140
If this was any other kind
of job, what would we do?

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:28.164
We'd try to figure out
what we were dealing with.

00:12:28.721 --> 00:12:31.270
We'd dig into the history
of the house. Exactly.

00:12:31.293 --> 00:12:32.835
Except this time we
already know what happened.

00:12:32.868 --> 00:12:36.479
Yeah, but how much do we know?
How much do you actually remember?

00:12:38.497 --> 00:12:40.382
About that night, you mean? Yeah.

00:12:42.335 --> 00:12:43.308
Not much.

00:12:44.766 --> 00:12:46.136
I remember the fire...

00:12:47.138 --> 00:12:48.037
The heat.

00:12:51.973 --> 00:12:53.475
Then I carried you out the front door.

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:57.070
You did?

00:12:58.897 --> 00:13:00.326
Yeah, well, you never knew that?

00:13:02.662 --> 00:13:03.507
No.

00:13:05.454 --> 00:13:06.456
And, uh...

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:09.020
Well, you know dad's story
as well as I do. Mom was...

00:13:10.567 --> 00:13:11.642
Was on the ceiling.

00:13:12.232 --> 00:13:14.957
Whatever put her there was long
gone by the time dad found her.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:18.694
And he never had a
theory about what did it?

00:13:19.201 --> 00:13:20.779
If he did, he kept it to himself.

00:13:21.693 --> 00:13:23.976
God knows we asked him enough times.

00:13:26.938 --> 00:13:27.778
Okay.

00:13:28.692 --> 00:13:31.211
So, if we're gonna figure
out what's going on now,

00:13:32.582 --> 00:13:34.394
We have to figure out
what happened back then,

00:13:35.676 --> 00:13:37.282
And see if it's the same thing.

00:13:37.444 --> 00:13:37.915
Yeah.

00:13:39.315 --> 00:13:42.416
Talk to dad's friends, neighbors,
people who were there at the time.

00:13:44.344 --> 00:13:46.654
Does this feel like
just another job to you?

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:55.162
I'll be right back. I
got to go to the bathroom.

00:14:13.828 --> 00:14:15.567
<i>This is John Winchester.</i>

00:14:15.639 --> 00:14:21.959
<i>If this is an emergency, call
my son Dean, 866 907 32 35.</i>

00:14:22.003 --> 00:14:22.519
Dad...

00:14:25.747 --> 00:14:28.210
I know I've left you messages before.

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:31.149
I don't even know if you get 'em.

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:34.720
But

00:14:35.192 --> 00:14:36.312
I'm with Sam

00:14:37.358 --> 00:14:38.905
And we're in Lawrence,

00:14:39.921 --> 00:14:42.359
And there's something in our old house.

00:14:43.693 --> 00:14:46.456
I don't know if it's the
thing that killed mom or not,

00:14:47.925 --> 00:14:48.352
But...

00:14:50.886 --> 00:14:52.775
I don't know what to do.

00:14:54.702 --> 00:14:55.483
So,

00:14:55.837 --> 00:14:58.108
Whatever you're doing,
if you could get here...

00:15:00.079 --> 00:15:00.949
Please.

00:15:03.588 --> 00:15:05.046
I need your help, dad.

00:15:10.145 --> 00:15:13.739
No, sir, nothing weird
down there. I promise.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:17.202
Sink just backed upon
its own. I'll take a look.

00:15:17.394 --> 00:15:18.321
Thanks.

00:15:19.456 --> 00:15:21.608
Oh, okay, I'll get out of your way.

00:17:04.791 --> 00:17:08.077
So you and John Winchester, you
used to own this garage together?

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:10.847
Yeah, we used to. A long time ago.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:11.844
Matter of fact,

00:17:12.065 --> 00:17:15.027
Must be 20 years since John disappeared.

00:17:15.171 --> 00:17:16.962
So, why are the cops
interested all of a sudden?

00:17:17.038 --> 00:17:21.046
Oh, we're reopening some of our unsolved cases,
and the Winchester disappearance is one of them.

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:23.755
Uh-Huh. Well, what do you
want to know about John?

00:17:23.849 --> 00:17:26.098
Whatever you remember, you know.
Whatever sticks out in your mind.

00:17:29.648 --> 00:17:32.319
He was a stubborn
bastard. I remember that.

00:17:33.297 --> 00:17:34.499
And, uh...

00:17:34.557 --> 00:17:37.466
Oh, whatever the game, he
hated to lose, you know?

00:17:37.502 --> 00:17:39.245
It was that whole marine thing.

00:17:40.293 --> 00:17:41.259
But, uh...

00:17:41.561 --> 00:17:43.010
Well, he sure loved Mary,

00:17:44.023 --> 00:17:45.518
And he doted on those kids.

00:17:46.001 --> 00:17:47.484
But that was before the fire.

00:17:48.577 --> 00:17:49.225
That's right.

00:17:49.543 --> 00:17:50.932
He ever talk about that night?

00:17:52.523 --> 00:17:53.120
No,

00:17:53.496 --> 00:17:54.545
Not at first.

00:17:55.239 --> 00:17:57.101
I think he was in shock. Right,

00:17:57.666 --> 00:17:59.067
But eventually,

00:18:00.139 --> 00:18:01.525
What did he say about it?

00:18:02.217 --> 00:18:05.066
Oh, he wasn't thinking
straight. He said, uh...

00:18:05.692 --> 00:18:09.191
He said something caused
that fire and killed Mary.

00:18:09.226 --> 00:18:10.260
He ever say what did it?

00:18:11.203 --> 00:18:13.732
Nothing did it. It was an accident.

00:18:14.135 --> 00:18:17.821
An electrical short in the
ceiling or walls or something.

00:18:19.776 --> 00:18:23.595
I begged him to get some
help, but... But what?

00:18:24.158 --> 00:18:26.030
Oh, it just got worse and worse.

00:18:26.242 --> 00:18:26.783
How?

00:18:27.514 --> 00:18:31.048
Oh, he started reading
these strange old books.

00:18:31.083 --> 00:18:33.809
He started going to see
this palm reader in town.

00:18:33.982 --> 00:18:36.113
Palm reader? You have a name?

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.173
No.

00:18:42.309 --> 00:18:45.754
All right, so, there are a few
psychics and palm readers in town.

00:18:45.789 --> 00:18:48.244
There's someone named
El Divino. There's...

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:51.189
There's the mysterious Mr. Fortinsky.

00:18:51.305 --> 00:18:53.955
Uh, Missouri Moseley,
some dude -- Wait, wait...

00:18:54.038 --> 00:18:55.169
Missouri Moseley?

00:18:55.498 --> 00:18:55.958
What?

00:18:56.275 --> 00:18:57.194
That's a psychic?

00:18:57.806 --> 00:19:00.515
Uh...yeah.Yeah, I guess so.

00:19:04.157 --> 00:19:05.064
In dad's journal...

00:19:08.468 --> 00:19:09.747
Look at this.

00:19:11.382 --> 00:19:13.793
First page, first sentence. Read that.

00:19:14.742 --> 00:19:16.073
"I went to Missouri...

00:19:17.333 --> 00:19:18.917
And I learned the truth."

00:19:19.747 --> 00:19:21.566
I always thought he meant the state.

00:19:27.402 --> 00:19:28.886
All right, then.

00:19:29.286 --> 00:19:31.253
Don't you worry about a thing.

00:19:32.065 --> 00:19:33.820
Your wife is crazy about you.

00:19:37.251 --> 00:19:39.900
Whew! Poor bastard.

00:19:40.406 --> 00:19:42.726
His woman cold-Bangin'the gardener.

00:19:43.887 --> 00:19:45.773
Why didn't you tell him?

00:19:46.169 --> 00:19:48.343
People don't come here for the truth.

00:19:48.379 --> 00:19:50.214
They come for good news.

00:19:51.727 --> 00:19:52.528
Well?

00:19:52.693 --> 00:19:55.965
Sam and Dean, come on
already. I ain't got all day.

00:20:04.112 --> 00:20:05.797
Well, let me look at you.

00:20:07.528 --> 00:20:10.556
Oh, you boys grew up handsome.

00:20:10.884 --> 00:20:14.050
And you were one
goofy-Looking kid, too.

00:20:15.816 --> 00:20:16.853
Sam.

00:20:19.785 --> 00:20:21.269
Oh, honey.

00:20:23.166 --> 00:20:26.345
I'm sorry about your girlfriend.

00:20:26.958 --> 00:20:28.600
And your father

00:20:30.299 --> 00:20:31.829
he's missing?

00:20:34.774 --> 00:20:36.414
How'd you know all that?

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:37.059
Well,

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:41.025
You were just thinking it, just now.

00:20:41.548 --> 00:20:43.474
Well, where is he? Is he okay?

00:20:44.104 --> 00:20:45.521
I don't know.

00:20:46.189 --> 00:20:47.202
Don't know?

00:20:48.273 --> 00:20:49.996
You're supposed to be a psychic, right?

00:20:50.664 --> 00:20:54.782
Boy, you see me sawing
some bony tramp in half?

00:20:54.817 --> 00:20:56.220
You think I'm a magician?

00:20:56.459 --> 00:20:59.584
I may be able to read thoughts
and sense energies in a room,

00:20:59.619 --> 00:21:01.816
But I can't just pull
facts out of thin air.

00:21:01.851 --> 00:21:02.291
Sit!

00:21:02.545 --> 00:21:03.177
Please.

00:21:13.308 --> 00:21:16.959
Boy, you put your foot on my coffee
table, I'm gonna whack you with a spoon.

00:21:16.994 --> 00:21:17.900
I didn't do anything.

00:21:17.986 --> 00:21:19.485
Well, you were thinking about it.

00:21:26.114 --> 00:21:27.756
Okay, so...

00:21:28.746 --> 00:21:29.519
Our dad.

00:21:30.386 --> 00:21:31.849
When did you first meet him?

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:33.945
He came for a reading

00:21:34.644 --> 00:21:37.406
A few days after the fire.

00:21:38.298 --> 00:21:41.669
I just told him what was
really out there in the dark.

00:21:41.815 --> 00:21:43.543
I guess you could say

00:21:44.814 --> 00:21:46.915
I drew back the curtains for him.

00:21:46.941 --> 00:21:48.026
What about the fire?

00:21:49.449 --> 00:21:52.102
Do you know about what killed our mom?

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:53.207
A little.

00:21:54.151 --> 00:21:56.305
Your daddy took me to your house.

00:21:56.479 --> 00:21:58.265
He was hoping I could

00:21:58.410 --> 00:21:59.475
Sense the

00:21:59.946 --> 00:22:00.955
Echoes,

00:22:00.993 --> 00:22:03.020
The fingerprints of this thing.

00:22:03.379 --> 00:22:04.330
And could you?

00:22:04.913 --> 00:22:05.686
I don't...

00:22:07.484 --> 00:22:08.427
What was it?

00:22:09.115 --> 00:22:10.096
I don't know.

00:22:12.962 --> 00:22:14.811
But it was evil.

00:22:15.024 --> 00:22:19.436
Look, I feel just awful
about the poor man's hand,

00:22:20.433 --> 00:22:23.114
But how can I be held liable?

00:22:25.486 --> 00:22:26.072
Yeah, but

00:22:26.231 --> 00:22:28.344
I can't afford a lawyer.

00:22:30.805 --> 00:22:33.526
Okay, listen, y-You just
got to let me call you back.

00:22:34.706 --> 00:22:37.759
Richie, mommy's gonna be right back,

00:22:37.985 --> 00:22:38.730
Okay?

00:22:38.825 --> 00:22:39.673
Okay.

00:22:40.098 --> 00:22:40.727
Okay.

00:22:44.857 --> 00:22:45.819
So,

00:22:47.373 --> 00:22:50.084
You think something's
back in that house?

00:22:51.053 --> 00:22:52.588
Definitely.

00:22:55.736 --> 00:22:57.543
I don't understand.

00:22:58.119 --> 00:22:59.277
What?

00:23:01.947 --> 00:23:03.766
I haven't been back inside,

00:23:03.801 --> 00:23:08.216
But I've been keeping an eye on
the place, and it's been quiet.

00:23:08.461 --> 00:23:10.568
No sudden deaths, no

00:23:10.730 --> 00:23:12.455
Freak accidents.

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:14.085
Why is it acting up now?

00:23:14.578 --> 00:23:15.435
I don't know.

00:23:16.175 --> 00:23:19.544
But dad going missing
and Jessica dying and

00:23:19.943 --> 00:23:21.503
Now this house,

00:23:22.016 --> 00:23:25.439
All happening at once. It just
feels like something's starting.

00:23:26.112 --> 00:23:28.245
That's a comforting thought.

00:23:59.416 --> 00:24:00.746
Juicy!

00:24:15.191 --> 00:24:19.087
Oh, baby, either we have
rats or mommy is going crazy.

00:24:19.804 --> 00:24:20.557
Richie?

00:24:23.302 --> 00:24:24.444
Richie?!

00:24:34.778 --> 00:24:37.125
Baby, where are you?!

00:24:45.490 --> 00:24:46.173
Wha...

00:24:54.314 --> 00:24:56.505
Mum! Oh, my god!

00:25:02.719 --> 00:25:03.896
Oh, baby!

00:25:06.972 --> 00:25:08.716
Sam, Dean,

00:25:09.092 --> 00:25:10.270
What are you doing here?

00:25:10.447 --> 00:25:11.542
Hey, Jenny.

00:25:11.813 --> 00:25:14.185
Um, this is our friend Missouri.

00:25:15.011 --> 00:25:18.361
If it's not too much trouble, we were
hoping to show her the house, you know,

00:25:18.525 --> 00:25:20.440
For old time's sake.

00:25:20.476 --> 00:25:22.739
No, you know, this isn't a good time.

00:25:22.774 --> 00:25:24.743
I'm kind of busy. Listen,
Jenny,it's important.

00:25:24.888 --> 00:25:25.379
Ow!

00:25:25.742 --> 00:25:29.074
Give the poor girl a break.
Can't you see she's upset?

00:25:29.109 --> 00:25:30.546
Forgive this boy. He means well.

00:25:30.581 --> 00:25:32.625
He's just not the
sharpest tool in the shed.

00:25:32.660 --> 00:25:34.047
But hear me out.

00:25:34.653 --> 00:25:35.764
About what?

00:25:35.822 --> 00:25:37.093
About this house.

00:25:37.891 --> 00:25:39.279
What are you talking about?

00:25:39.776 --> 00:25:42.515
I think you know what I'm talking about.

00:25:42.550 --> 00:25:47.501
You think there's something in this house,
something that wants to hurt your family.

00:25:47.536 --> 00:25:48.996
Am I mistaken?

00:25:49.933 --> 00:25:51.677
Who are you?

00:25:51.712 --> 00:25:54.994
We're people who can help,
who can stop this thing,

00:25:55.029 --> 00:25:57.492
But you're gonna have to
trust us, just a little.

00:26:00.224 --> 00:26:05.449
If there's a dark energy around here,
this room should be the center of it.

00:26:06.804 --> 00:26:07.618
Why?

00:26:08.150 --> 00:26:10.838
This used to be your nursery, Sam.

00:26:10.873 --> 00:26:13.158
This is where it all happened.

00:26:28.508 --> 00:26:30.192
That an emf?

00:26:30.588 --> 00:26:31.176
Yeah.

00:26:32.140 --> 00:26:32.990
Amateur.

00:26:43.397 --> 00:26:46.246
I don't know if you boys should
be disappointed or relieved,

00:26:46.281 --> 00:26:48.471
But this ain't the
thing that took your mom.

00:26:50.138 --> 00:26:51.572
Are you sure?

00:26:52.557 --> 00:26:53.787
How do you know?

00:26:53.794 --> 00:26:57.611
It isn't the same energy I
felt the last time I was here.

00:26:57.646 --> 00:26:59.064
It's something different.

00:27:00.053 --> 00:27:01.079
What is it?

00:27:02.714 --> 00:27:04.211
Not it...

00:27:04.972 --> 00:27:06.522
Them.

00:27:07.139 --> 00:27:10.218
There's more than one
spirit in this place.

00:27:11.379 --> 00:27:12.997
What are they doing here?

00:27:13.032 --> 00:27:15.903
They're here because of
what happened to your family.

00:27:16.499 --> 00:27:18.409
You see, all those years ago,

00:27:18.501 --> 00:27:21.051
Real evil came to you.

00:27:22.437 --> 00:27:27.049
It walked this house. That
kind of evil leaves wounds,

00:27:27.085 --> 00:27:29.869
And sometimes wounds get infected.

00:27:30.186 --> 00:27:31.925
I don't understand.

00:27:31.960 --> 00:27:35.248
This place is a magnet
for paranormal energy.

00:27:38.073 --> 00:27:40.493
It's attracted a poltergeist,

00:27:40.950 --> 00:27:42.630
A nasty one,

00:27:43.400 --> 00:27:47.176
And it won't rest until
Jenny and her babies are dead.

00:27:47.211 --> 00:27:49.449
You said there was more than one spirit.

00:27:49.538 --> 00:27:51.047
There is.

00:27:53.919 --> 00:27:57.229
I just can't quite
make out the second one.

00:28:01.305 --> 00:28:03.157
Well, one thing's for damn sure,

00:28:03.747 --> 00:28:05.591
Nobody's dying in this house,

00:28:05.627 --> 00:28:06.770
Ever again.

00:28:07.453 --> 00:28:09.813
So, whatever is here, how do we stop it?

00:28:13.241 --> 00:28:15.370
So, what is all this stuff anyway?

00:28:15.813 --> 00:28:19.266
Angelica root, van van
oil, crossroad dirt,

00:28:19.321 --> 00:28:21.265
A few other odds and ends.

00:28:21.300 --> 00:28:22.534
What are we supposed to do with it?

00:28:22.569 --> 00:28:25.754
We're gonna put them inside the walls

00:28:25.971 --> 00:28:29.216
In the north, south, east, west corners

00:28:29.251 --> 00:28:31.191
On each floor of the house.

00:28:31.226 --> 00:28:34.346
Punching holes in the drywall.
Jenny's gonna love that.

00:28:35.310 --> 00:28:36.733
She'll live.

00:28:37.805 --> 00:28:40.057
And this will destroy the spirits?

00:28:40.092 --> 00:28:41.374
It should.

00:28:41.947 --> 00:28:44.578
It should purify the house completely.

00:28:45.726 --> 00:28:47.398
We'll each take a floor,

00:28:47.763 --> 00:28:49.279
But we work fast.

00:28:49.314 --> 00:28:52.187
Once the spirits
realize what we're up to,

00:28:52.215 --> 00:28:54.354
Things are gonna get bad.

00:28:56.132 --> 00:28:56.988
Okay.

00:28:58.323 --> 00:28:59.712
Careful.

00:29:01.221 --> 00:29:05.046
Look, I -You know, I'm not sure I'm
comfortable leaving you guys here alone.

00:29:05.081 --> 00:29:07.389
Just take your kids to
the movie or something, and

00:29:07.428 --> 00:29:09.590
It'll be over by the time you get back.

00:29:10.466 --> 00:29:11.160
Okay.

00:30:08.072 --> 00:30:09.830
Aah! Uhh!

00:30:48.041 --> 00:30:48.819
Sam!

00:30:51.139 --> 00:30:51.881
Sam!

00:31:14.995 --> 00:31:16.192
Come on.

00:31:38.055 --> 00:31:39.948
Are you sure this is over?

00:31:43.130 --> 00:31:44.445
I'm sure.

00:31:44.875 --> 00:31:45.486
Why?

00:31:46.641 --> 00:31:48.334
Why do you ask?

00:31:49.193 --> 00:31:50.790
No, never mind.

00:31:52.502 --> 00:31:54.357
It's nothing, I guess.

00:31:56.401 --> 00:31:57.729
Hello?

00:31:58.308 --> 00:31:59.793
We're home.

00:32:02.842 --> 00:32:04.457
What happened?

00:32:04.561 --> 00:32:07.243
Hi. Sorry. Um, we'll...

00:32:07.278 --> 00:32:09.316
We'll pay for all of this.

00:32:10.081 --> 00:32:11.519
Don't you worry.

00:32:11.577 --> 00:32:13.651
Dean's gonna clean up this mess.

00:32:16.689 --> 00:32:18.680
Well, what are you waiting for, boy?

00:32:18.715 --> 00:32:19.486
Get the mop.

00:32:20.394 --> 00:32:21.960
And don't cuss at me.

00:32:43.576 --> 00:32:44.342
Okay.

00:33:38.518 --> 00:33:40.631
So, tell me again. What
are we still doing here?

00:33:40.666 --> 00:33:42.133
I don't know, I-I just...

00:33:42.781 --> 00:33:44.371
I still have a bad feeling.

00:33:44.960 --> 00:33:45.973
Why?

00:33:46.491 --> 00:33:50.150
Missouri did her whole zelda rubenstein thing.
The house should be clean. This should be over.

00:33:50.376 --> 00:33:53.297
Yeah, probably, but I just
want to make sure. That's all.

00:33:54.767 --> 00:33:57.835
The problem is I could be
sleeping in a bed right now.

00:34:02.224 --> 00:34:03.165
Dean!

00:34:03.648 --> 00:34:04.351
Dean!

00:34:06.318 --> 00:34:08.169
You grab the kids, I'll get Jenny.

00:34:26.903 --> 00:34:28.611
Come on! Jenny!

00:34:28.649 --> 00:34:31.278
I can't open the door! Stand back!

00:34:34.356 --> 00:34:35.863
Come on! No, my kids!

00:34:35.870 --> 00:34:36.994
Sam's got your kids. Come on.

00:34:39.758 --> 00:34:40.856
Help!

00:34:41.516 --> 00:34:42.634
Please!

00:34:46.261 --> 00:34:47.380
Come here.

00:34:48.084 --> 00:34:49.682
Don't look, don't look.

00:35:03.084 --> 00:35:06.385
Sari, take your brother outside as
fast as you can and don't look back.

00:35:14.704 --> 00:35:16.300
Are you okay, baby?

00:35:16.323 --> 00:35:19.194
Sari, where's Sam? He's
inside. Something's got him.

00:35:41.555 --> 00:35:43.485
Ugh! Aah!

00:36:06.625 --> 00:36:07.205
Sam!

00:36:28.019 --> 00:36:28.853
Sam?!

00:36:29.758 --> 00:36:30.285
Sam!

00:36:35.059 --> 00:36:37.206
No, don't! Don't! What? Why?

00:36:38.524 --> 00:36:40.010
Because I know who it is.

00:36:40.789 --> 00:36:42.514
I can see her now.

00:36:59.709 --> 00:37:01.050
Mom.

00:37:11.406 --> 00:37:12.717
Dean.

00:37:28.125 --> 00:37:29.581
Sam.

00:37:36.085 --> 00:37:37.749
I'm sorry.

00:37:42.488 --> 00:37:44.156
F-For what?

00:37:56.513 --> 00:37:59.389
You, get out of my house.

00:38:00.210 --> 00:38:02.538
And let go of my son.

00:38:32.866 --> 00:38:34.444
Now it's over.

00:38:48.218 --> 00:38:49.477
Thanks for these.

00:38:49.991 --> 00:38:52.103
Don't thank me. They're yours.

00:38:56.833 --> 00:38:57.710
Well,

00:38:58.191 --> 00:39:01.802
There are no spirits in there
anymore, this time for sure.

00:39:02.990 --> 00:39:04.670
Not even my mom?

00:39:05.338 --> 00:39:06.678
No.

00:39:11.053 --> 00:39:12.548
What happened?

00:39:13.599 --> 00:39:18.274
Your mom's spirit and the poltergeists'
energy, they canceled each other out.

00:39:18.766 --> 00:39:22.370
Your mom destroyed herself
going after the thing.

00:39:23.632 --> 00:39:25.902
Why would she do something like that?

00:39:26.954 --> 00:39:30.045
Well, to protect her boys, of course.

00:39:37.952 --> 00:39:39.956
Sam, I'm sorry.

00:39:42.319 --> 00:39:43.714
For what?

00:39:44.246 --> 00:39:47.120
You sensed it was here, didn't you?

00:39:47.155 --> 00:39:48.887
Even when I couldn't.

00:39:53.915 --> 00:39:55.673
What's happening to me?

00:39:56.640 --> 00:39:59.654
I know I should have
all the answers, but...

00:40:01.362 --> 00:40:02.794
I don't know.

00:40:03.371 --> 00:40:04.819
Sam, you ready ?

00:40:09.900 --> 00:40:11.034
Bye.

00:40:14.039 --> 00:40:15.420
Bye Sam.

00:40:17.941 --> 00:40:19.106
Ah.

00:40:19.789 --> 00:40:22.140
Don't you boys be strangers.

00:40:22.564 --> 00:40:23.802
We won't.

00:40:25.356 --> 00:40:26.615
See you around.

00:40:58.047 --> 00:40:59.651
That boy...

00:41:01.289 --> 00:41:03.177
He has such

00:41:03.269 --> 00:41:05.272
Powerful abilities.

00:41:09.062 --> 00:41:11.810
Why he couldn't sense his own father,

00:41:12.023 --> 00:41:13.647
I have no idea.

00:41:19.423 --> 00:41:20.564
Mary's spirit...

00:41:22.364 --> 00:41:24.676
Do you really think she saved the boys?

00:41:27.024 --> 00:41:27.977
I do.

00:41:40.008 --> 00:41:42.742
John Winchester, I could just slap you.

00:41:42.808 --> 00:41:45.272
Why don't you go talk to your children?

00:41:46.910 --> 00:41:48.428
God, I want to.

00:41:50.421 --> 00:41:52.929
You have no idea how
much I want to see them.

00:41:55.881 --> 00:41:56.839
But I can't.

00:41:58.508 --> 00:41:59.216
Not yet.

00:42:05.782 --> 00:42:07.564
Not until I know the truth.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.231
